# Citation metadata for AUPHORIA.
#
# Authors are people only (no AI tools are authors). Abdul Momin Muhammad
# Wisal is the project creator and lead, and the only author listed. All
# contributors are credited in CONTRIBUTORS.md. The other four people are kept
# in a commented block below until each of their [CONFIRM ROLE] markers is
# replaced with the approved role/descriptor - do not uncomment them before
# then.
#
# doi and repository-code keep placeholders until a DOI is minted (Zenodo).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AUPHORIA in your research or coursework, please cite it as follows."
title: "AUPHORIA"
abstract: "AUPHORIA is an open-source, beginner-friendly data analysis tool for university students who cannot code. It runs offline on a student's own computer or in Google Colab, offers a menu of analyses that fit their data, and produces reproducible reports."
authors:
  - family-names: "Wisal"
    given-names: "Abdul Momin Muhammad"
    email: "ammw@aup.edu.pk"
# ---- Uncomment ONE entry at a time only after replacing each [CONFIRM ROLE]
# ---- with the approved role/descriptor (see CONTRIBUTORS.md).
#  - family-names: "Haq"
#    given-names: "Ihtesham Ul"
#    # [CONFIRM ROLE] Dr. Ihtesham Ul Haq - originator of the idea; reviewed and supervised.
#  - family-names: "Khan"
#    given-names: "Sher Hayat"
#    # [CONFIRM ROLE] Dr. Sher Hayat Khan - reviewed and supervised.
#  - family-names: "Moheb"
#    given-names: "Ahmad Farid"
#    # [CONFIRM ROLE] Ahmad Farid Moheb - MPhil research student; helped refine the idea and tested it; research focus: [CONFIRM].
#  - family-names: "Anayat"
#    given-names: "Mudassir"
#    # [CONFIRM ROLE] Mudassir Anayat - MPhil research student (epidemiology of Theileria annulata infection in dairy cattle); helped refine the idea and tested it; suggested testing focus (pending approval): prevalence and risk-factor analyses [CONFIRM].
keywords:
  - statistics
  - data analysis
  - education
  - research methods
  - reproducible research
date-released: "2026-10-29"
version: "0.1.0"
